\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Definition}
\title{Path transport in scalar frames}
\date{2026-11-19}

\p{Let #{\gamma} be an edge path from #{y} to #{x} in the
\vocabk{orbit gauge–Higgs weight}{fdip-010A}. Its transport
#{U_\gamma} is the ordered product of the traversed links, with
the first traversed link acting first. A backward traversal uses
the inverse link and an empty path has identity transport. For the
\vocabk{scalar frame}{fdip-010X} at each endpoint, the
\newvocab{framed path transport} is the group element
#{g_x^{-1}U_\gamma g_y}.}

\p{Suppose the scalar module has a #{G}-invariant #{k}-bilinear
pairing. The \newvocab{scalar path pairing} is the coefficient
#{\langle\phi_x,U_\gamma\phi_y\rangle\in k}. A closed path based
at #{x} still has a distinguished endpoint frame.}
